<p>This is definitely a start. I'm working on a concept myself so I understand how difficult it is to develop the story. Right now it is still a bit basic, but you are heading in the right direction</p>
<p><strong>Incident 1- Port opinions:</strong> Not too shabby. More detail as to what happens with the workers may assist the narrative.</p>
<p><strong>Incident 2 - Nuclear Plant opinions:</strong> I'm a bit confused as to how the organism made its way to the power plant? However, this has narrative potential too.</p>
<p><strong>Overall:</strong> I need to ask, what is the <em>main</em> narrative focus? You have a neat anomaly but what's the story with it? You've got some nice smaller narratives with the incidents, so perhaps exploring how the port workers dealt with the effects of the anomaly could be interesting? Like trying to fight against it.</p>
<p>The nuclear plant incident could be a story on its own as well if you put enough focus in it. Exploring how the spores caused shit to hit the fan. Both incidents have potential, and it's fully up to you to decide what you wanna do.</p>

