<blockquote>
<p>The broadcaster seems to want to help improve the organizations by critiquing them</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If he's some generic overpowered &quot;ethereal presence&quot;, and also a literal god, why does he have specific interest in this small niche of organizations compared to literally any other population of large corporations in the world?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This was meant to he a humorous article so feel free to give recommendations on improvements.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You're definitely going to need to make the motives more clear and relatable so the guy feels like a believable character and not just a plot device for making GoIs angry. Also, I feel like you're going to need to tone down how overpowered and untouchable the guy is, since &quot;my super powerful OC gives hot takes on your favorite GoIs and no one can stop him&quot; is probably not going to read as humor so much as an authorial power trip.</p>

