														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838296">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>ConProcs</li>
<li>Description</li>
<li>Discovery Log</li>
<li>List of SCP-Events</li>
<li>Testing Logs</li>
<li>Interview and Final Word from O5</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>You're home alone, watching the tv of your country. You hear a noise in the other room and go to investigate. You see nothing but the American flag planted firmly in the center of the room.</p>
<p>Then a voice whispers to you</p>
<p>&quot;God bless America&quot;.</p>
<p>And then you start a revolution.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>-<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/marcelles-raynes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5722579); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5722579&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607308113" alt="Marcelles_Raynes" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5722579)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/marcelles-raynes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5722579); return false;">Marcelles_Raynes</a></span> 12/4/2020</strong></p>
<p>1 out of every 5,000 American flags is a sentient petal of an extra-dimensional plant that symbiotically infects humans (mostly foreigners) and puppets them into influencing the political state of America with non-anomalous memetic strategies.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Story&nbsp;and&nbsp;Hook&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Story&nbsp;and&nbsp;Hook&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The first American flag, the original progenitor of this SCP, inspired the American Revolution only because the east coast was the perfect habitat for it to grow. The anomaly successfully thrived in America for centuries undetected, keeping their percentage of American hosts lower than the percentage of non-American hosts globally. And while these flags are too light to stop the wind from pushing them around outside, inside the human body they can morph themselves into microscopic threads to navigate, manipulate their hosts, and avoid detection.</p>
<p>It isn’t until 2015, when the Bundy standoff between the BLM and the ATF revealed a new progenitor flag attempting to start another revolution, that the Foundation identifies the presence of the anomaly. While the Foundation realizes complete containment of the anomaly would force them and the US into open war, they also discover that the anomaly has been defending humanity from numerous shape-shifting anomalies in secret, making itself essential to their needs too. They accept that the anomaly cannot and does not need to be actively contained, so, with caution, they focus on the threat of wild American flags going rogue and starting a new America all over again.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Inspired by a comment made by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/marcelles-raynes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5722579); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5722579&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607308113" alt="Marcelles_Raynes" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5722579)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/marcelles-raynes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5722579); return false;">Marcelles_Raynes</a></span> 's perspective on the phrase “God Bless America,” this SCP focuses on highlighting and mocking much of American flavored jingoism while not explaining it all off as something completely unnatural.</p>
<p>Johnny Appleseed, tea dumping in the Boston river, the start of the Spanish-American war, Westerns, and others are given are both humorous and unsettling examples. Test logs show how flags choose/infect their host and how infected hosts take down other shape-shifting threats (hint: think of a &quot;pulling a handkerchief out of the mouth&quot; magic trick but deadly.) Also hints at the end about what might have O5 worried most of all about the anomalies freedom.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The title is supposed to be the genus and species name but correct me if I got the order or idea wrong. Thanks!</p>

							</div>

								
					
