														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838285">
									

<p><em>I cannot greenlight nor can I provide expert critique</em></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open&nbsp;the&nbsp;critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close&nbsp;it</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Hello, regarding your concept: it is clearly over the 400 word limit so I'd suggest that you make it concise to allow the person critiquing your concept a more brief summary of your concept. I'd also think that you should remove unnecessary detail from the concept as this can come later when you have the draft critiqued. What I think should be omitted is:</p>
<blockquote>
<ul>
<li>Glomeromycota (We don't need to know exactly what genus it is at this stage)</li>
<li>entirely new bioluminescent fungi (You've mentioned several times of the bioluminescence of the fungi, you'd needn't more explanation it'd be best just to leave it as fungi for the rest of the concept)</li>
<li>specifying the latitudes of the Tropics is unnecessary at this stage and would be better suited in the draft</li>
<li>there isn't a need to include footnotes at this stage such as with &quot;artificial selection&quot; and ATP which is an acronym but is unnecessarily abbreviated (this does add more text however it seems to better for context)</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd also like to point out your classification of different parts of your concept. Labelling them as</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1a through to 1d</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this isn't necessary for the extra letters and you'd more likely useSCP-XXXX-1 through 4 instead.</p>
<p>Using the site director as a central narrative seems unprofessional due to the fact you labelled shortcomings in his work and the fact your attention grabber is the failing of the foundation to contain it and would present the foundation as an unprofessional group of people although this may work for some site staff it wouldn't be for most of them.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Send a wikidot pm if you update it because I'd love to critique it again when it's been modified</p>

